Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Continuous Quantum Measurement, from Bayes\[CloseCurlyQuote] Rule to the \
Quantum Kalman Filter\
\>", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9949616046166563`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-\
3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
In this computational essay, we explore a quantum particle whose position is \
monitored continuously. This is what is usually called continuous weak \
measurement. It starts from the stochastic Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation \
(the SDE that drives a state while it is being measured), turns the \
measurement step into ordinary Bayesian updating, and runs the whole thing on \
a position grid with a Trotter-Suzuki splitting scheme. We focus on two \
examples in particular. A free particle, where the measurement narrows a \
spread-out state to a packet of finite steady width and the noisy measurement \
record alone tells you where it settled. And a harmonic trap, where \
continuous measurement squeezes the position variance below the ground \
state's, and the quantum Kalman filter that levitated-nanoparticle and \
membrane experiments actually run rebuilds the conditional mean position from \
the noisy signal.\
\>", "Abstract",ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami. Last updated August 4, 2026.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part I: The Equation of Motion, and Measurement as Bayes' Rule\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Start with the equation of motion. A particle with Hamiltonian ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 " whose position is measured continuously and weakly obeys a stochastic Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation (SSE), the diffusive quantum-state-diffusion \
form,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        FractionBox[
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[HBar]"]}], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
       SuperscriptBox[
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["(",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
         RowBox[{
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           OverscriptBox[
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
           StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
         StyleBox[")",
          FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], "2"], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "+", 
      RowBox[{
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1], 
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
           SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]}], "]"}], 
    RowBox[{
     TemplateBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
      "Ket"], "."}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In words: the first term is ordinary unitary evolution under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 "; the last is the stochastic measurement backaction, proportional to the \
Wiener increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " (an independent Gaussian of mean zero and variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " in each step), which nudges the state toward a sharper position; and the \
middle term is the nonlinear drift whose only job is to keep ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " normalized. The strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " sets how fast position information arrives, and its dimensions (inverse \
length squared, per time) say what kind of rate it is: what accrues is not \
position but statistical distinguishability: the log-likelihood ratio between \
two candidate positions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 " apart grows at the rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " (equivalently their Kullback-Leibler rate), a fact Part III will watch in \
action. (Factor conventions for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 " and for the record differ across the literature by twos; translate \
parameters before comparing formulas across sources.) The detector's own \
output over the same increment is the measurement record"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which is the conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " buried in white noise. Equivalently, the record is signal (the mean) plus \
shot noise (the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "W"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 "). Because that one increment drives both the state and the record, an \
observer who knows the initial state can feed the record into the same \
dynamics and track the conditional state as the experiment runs, never seeing \
the wavefunction directly. That is quantum filtering, and it is what a real \
experiment computes, in software, from the detector's streaming output. Part \
IV does it concretely, and there the record fixes the conditional mean while \
the width follows a rule that never looks at the record."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
Keep one piece of bookkeeping straight from the start. In an experiment only \
the record is data; the conditional state, its mean, and its width are \
inferences from that data through an assumed model. In this essay even the \
record is synthetic, generated by the same equations that propagate the \
state, so whenever two of our computed objects agree below, the agreement is \
an internal consistency check of the model, never evidence for it. What \
evidence for the model itself looks like in a laboratory, whiteness tests on \
the filter's surprises and independent out-of-loop calibration, appears at \
the close of Part IV.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The above SSE is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " limit of a concrete two-step update, and it is the update, not the \
differential form, that the simulation runs. Over one step the detector \
returns a single weak-measurement outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 ", a reading of the position blurred by Gaussian noise, and the state is \
revised by ",
 StyleBox["Bayes' rule",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". The reading has likelihood"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", "2", 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "a Gaussian in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " centered on the candidate position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ". (The dropped constant is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{"2", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[Pi]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 "; it cancels in the normalized update below, and needs restoring only if ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],
 " is read as a normalized density rather than a reweighting factor.) Because \
the reading is noisy, the outcome is not drawn from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " directly but from the ",
 StyleBox["prior predictive", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ", the density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " convolved with the detector noise. And the conditional (posterior) density \
is the prior reweighted by the likelihood,"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "\[ThickSpace]", "\[LongRightArrow]",
     "\[ThickSpace]", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThickSpace]", 
      SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
         {
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
           StyleBox["(",
            SpanMaxSize->1], 
           StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
           StyleBox[")",
            SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
        },
        GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
        GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "which is Bayes' rule verbatim: posterior ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Proportional]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Times]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " prior. At the level of amplitudes this reweighting is a Kraus operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", the square root of the likelihood, applied and renormalized; multiplying \
each amplitude by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "\[VerticalSeparator]", 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " carries the phase along. The particle then evolves unitarily for the step, \
so one full step is Bayes' rule followed by Hamiltonian evolution:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox[
       StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
        StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      TemplateBox[{
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
       "Ket"]}], GridBox[{
       {GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            OverscriptBox[
             StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             StyleBox["(",
              SpanMaxSize->1], 
             OverscriptBox[
              StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
             StyleBox[")",
              SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
            TemplateBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
                StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
                StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
                StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
             "Ket"]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "."}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In short: measure by Bayes' rule, then evolve. (The ordering is a \
discretization, not physics: over a real interval the two proceed together, \
and splitting them costs an error first order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 "; Part III puts a number on it.) Notice the one fact we will lean on for \
the rest of the notebook: the measurement half of this update knows nothing \
about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 ". The outcome distribution, the Bayesian reweighting, and the \
renormalization are identical for a free particle or a trap; only the unitary \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],
 " carries the potential. So generalizing the simulation to any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " will mean generalizing that one factor and leaving the measurement \
untouched, which is exactly what the next Part does."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Glossary", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The symbols of this Part sort into what a detector records and what an \
observer infers from it. What a detector actually returns is finite, one \
number per time step ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 ", so here we write those recorded increments with ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalDelta]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 "; the continuous ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 "-forms of the equations above (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 ") are their ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "\[Rule]", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " idealizations, living only inside the model. The last column gives each \
symbol's standing: recorded, calibrated from the record, or inferred through \
the model."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Symbol", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
     Cell["Meaning", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
     Cell["Standing, and how it is checked", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the measurement record over one step, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"], 
    Cell["\<\
Recorded: the detector's output each step, the only raw data here.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
      StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"], Cell[TextData[{
     "one weak-measurement outcome per step, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "/", 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{"2", 
        SqrtBox[
         StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"], 
    Cell[TextData[{
     "Calibrated from the record, not a separate reading: the same ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
     " in position units. One reading is mostly noise."
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the conditional mean position, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Integral]",
        FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
       SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
          {
           RowBox[{
            StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["(",
             SpanMaxSize->1], 
            StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
            StyleBox[")",
             SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
         },
         GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
         GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
       StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"], 
    Cell["\<\
Inferred: the filter of Part IV reconstructs it from the record, and feedback \
acts on it.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"]},
   {Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
     FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
     "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"], Cell[TextData[{
     "the shot-noise increment (variance ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
     "), the record minus the mean, ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
       SqrtBox[
        StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
       StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
        SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
      FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
      "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"], 
    Cell["\<\
Inferred: the record minus the estimated mean. If this leftover is not pure \
noise, the model is wrong.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"]}
  },
  GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}},
  GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
  GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {
      Scaled[0.14], 
      Scaled[0.37], 
      Scaled[0.37]}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
  GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.5}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}]], "Text",Express\
ionUUID->"b71e54b4-c252-4547-b096-11427f6a4708"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Only the record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " is recorded; the outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],
 " is that same increment calibrated into position units, and the conditional \
mean ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],
 " is inferred from the whole record by filtering, which is exactly what Part \
IV shows a real experiment doing in real time."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Part II: Simulating Any Potential on a Grid", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Part I gave the update as an equation; to run it we have to make one \
decision that everything else follows from. A wavefunction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " is defined at every point of the infinite line, which is more than a \
computer can hold, so we keep it only on a finite grid: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 " equally spaced points across a window of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],
 ", at spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 ". The state becomes a list of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " complex numbers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 ", and every operation below is arithmetic on that list. The care is all in \
choosing the window and the spacing, and in carrying, next to the positions, \
the momenta we will need. Let me explain each piece before writing the grid."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why a periodic box.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " Cutting space to a window of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 " leaves two loose ends, and we glue them: the point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " is identified with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "+", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 ", so the segment becomes a ring of circumference ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],
 ". We choose this periodic boundary for one reason. Momentum states are the \
plane waves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 ", and on a ring such a wave is allowed only if it closes up smoothly after \
going once around, which forces the momentum onto the discrete ladder"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]"}], 
     StyleBox["L", "TI"]], " ", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "\[Ellipsis]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", "1"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In other words, periodicity is exactly what turns momentum from a continuum \
into an evenly spaced list we can store beside the positions, and it makes \
those plane waves an exact basis. It costs nothing as long as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " stays negligible at the edges, so the packet never feels the seam where \
the ends are glued."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How to choose the length and the spacing.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " must be large enough to hold the whole wavefunction, tails included, for \
the entire run: the packet spreads, drifts, and (under measurement) heats, \
and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " must contain all of it, or a tail that reaches one edge reappears at the \
other. The spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " must be small enough to resolve the fastest wiggle of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", which is set by its largest momentum: a component of momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 " oscillates with de Broglie wavelength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 " (we keep the symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],
 " for the measurement strength), and capturing a wave needs at least two \
samples across it, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 " small enough that the biggest momentum you expect stays below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 ". The two ends are mirror images: the box length fixes the momentum spacing \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],
 " (fine momentum needs a big box), the sampling fixes the momentum reach ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],
 " (high momentum needs fine sampling). So choosing the position grid already \
fixes the momentum grid."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["What the Fourier transform is, and why we want it.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " We will keep switching between two descriptions of the same state: how \
much amplitude sits at each position, the list ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 ", and how much sits at each momentum, the coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],
 " when we write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 " as a sum of the plane waves above, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 ". The recipe that turns the first list into the second is the ",
 StyleBox["Fourier transform", "TI"],
 ": a reversible change of basis, the fixed sum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", 
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " that correlates the state against each plane wave, with an inverse that \
rebuilds ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ". (The built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData["Fourier"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],
 " refers phases to the first grid point rather than to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],
 ", which multiplies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],
 " by a per-mode sign; it cancels in every round trip below and in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["How a wavefunction sits on the grid.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " After all that, representing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 " is the easy part: evaluate it at the grid points and normalize, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "\[Function]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "1"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "=", "1"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 ". The normalization makes each entry carry a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],
 ": the list stores ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " is probability per grid point rather than a density, and every expectation \
below is a plain dot product for exactly that reason. That list is the state \
in the position description; its Fourier transform is the same state in the \
momentum description. First fix units so that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"hbar", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"mass", " ", "=", " ", "1"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the grid given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 " the space and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["l", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " the size of the box:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "l_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"dx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"l", "/", "n"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"<|", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<dx\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "dx"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<x\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{"dx", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "     ", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<p\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hbar", "/", "l"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{"RotateLeft", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "n"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"n", "/", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The grid itself returns an association with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],
 ", the spacing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "x"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 ", the positions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "{", "-", 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", "2", "-", "1", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " (centered on the origin, so the box is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], "/", "2"}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 "), and the quantized momenta ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", "2", "\[Pi]", "\[HBar]", " ", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["L", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],
 ". The momenta are stored rotated, nonnegative ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],
 " first and the negative half moved to the end, because that is the order ",
 Cell[BoxData["Fourier"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " returns them in, so that later one multiplication lands each amplitude on \
its own momentum. Fix the transform's sign convention once, as a pair used \
everywhere below:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Fourier", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"ift", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"InverseFourier", "[", 
    RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FourierParameters", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A convenient initial state is a Gaussian wave packet centered at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 " with mean momentum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "0"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 " and position width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],
 ". Following the recipe just above, we write its formula on the grid points ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " and normalize:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "x0_", ",", " ", "p0_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], 
   " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "x0"}], ")"}],
          "^", "2"}]}], "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"4", " ", 
         RowBox[{"s", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", "p0", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "/", "hbar"}]}]}], "]"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two numbers we will watch most are the conditional mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Integral]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["(",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[")",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], " ", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],
 " and the conditional variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 ". On the grid each is a dot product against the probability density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", ".", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the measurement step, we implement it in the two pieces: first the \
outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ", then the Bayesian update of the state."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The outcome ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " is a sample from the prior predictive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 ". Recall that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],
 " convolved with Gaussian noise of variance ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],
 ". So for the sampling of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],
 ", we can treat it as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], "=", 
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],
 ", with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],
 " distributed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Xi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],
 " distributed as a Gaussian with zero mean and standard deviation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"drawSyntheticOutcome", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The intermediate draw ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " is a sampling device for that convolution, nothing more: it is discarded \
on the spot, and no position is thereby assigned to the particle; only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " leaves the detector. (",
 Cell[BoxData["drawSyntheticOutcome"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],
 " is exact in that sense: it samples the finite-step outcome law without \
approximation.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Second the Bayesian update itself: reweight the amplitudes by the square \
root of the likelihood, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],
 ", and renormalize. That is the whole measurement step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", " ", "xb_"}],
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Lambda]"}], " ", "dt", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "xb"}], ")"}], 
        "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "(One numerical caveat for reuse: a wildly off-center ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 ", or a very strong measurement, can drive every weight below machine range \
before ",
 Cell[BoxData["Normalize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 ", which would then return a zero vector; at the strengths here that never \
bites, but a hardened version subtracts the peak exponent before \
exponentiating.)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Is this really Bayes' rule? It should be: the updated density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"p", "o", "s", "t"}], "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],
 " ought to equal the prior ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],
 " times the likelihood ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", "2", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "-", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"]}], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 ", normalized. Confirm the two constructions agree, for a test state and \
outcome:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gDemo", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
       RowBox[{"512", ",", " ", "40."}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "=", " ", ".75"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", ".01"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"xb", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"-", ".5"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Psi]t", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gDemo", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.5", ",", " ", "2."}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"post", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
              RowBox[{
              "gDemo", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", 
               "xb"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]t", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",",
          "\n", "    ", 
         RowBox[{"bayes", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", "dt", " ", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"gDemo", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
                  "xb"}], ")"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]t", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
            "Total"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"post", " ", "-", " ", "bayes"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],

Cell[BoxData["1.734723475976807`*^-17"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9949617364672403`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[10]=",ExpressionUUID->"339e1f03-09a6-4549-b4f9-84c30b7e0663"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The difference is at machine level, so ",
 Cell[BoxData["measUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " is exactly the Bayesian posterior; the operator form and the \"likelihood \
times prior\" form are two representations of the same update."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],

Cell["\<\
Before the runs themselves, two one-line helpers they will need.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Later we discard the record and average over the noise, and that average is \
not a single state vector but a blend of many, written as a density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],
 ". Those runs start from the pure initial state in that form, the outer \
product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 ", which ",
 Cell[BoxData["KroneckerProduct"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 " builds in one step; for a state of length ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],
 " it is also the projector onto ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],
 ", which is where the name comes from:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"projector", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Psi]", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The other helper checks the arithmetic: nothing the engine does should \
change a state's length, so the norm error, how far ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {GridBox[{
       {
        TemplateBox[{
          StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
         "Ket"]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.22}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " has slipped from ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ", should never rise above the floating-point floor:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"normError", "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],

Cell["\<\
Two more checks catch the two ways a finite grid can quietly lie. The box is \
a ring, so probability that reaches the wall wraps around to the far side; \
and the grid holds only a limited span of momenta, so probability that \
reaches the fastest ones can no longer be told from slow motion. Both stay \
harmless only while the packet keeps clear of those edges, so we measure how \
much probability has reached each: the outer tenth of the box, and the \
fastest tenth of the momenta. Both are the same sum over the outer tenth of \
an axis, so define that once as a helper and apply it to the position and to \
the momentum:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{"coord_", ",", " ", "probs_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "@", 
    RowBox[{"Pick", "[", 
     RowBox[{"probs", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"UnitStep", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "coord", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0.9", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
          RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "coord", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1"}], 
     "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"edgeMass", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"tailMass", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "\[Psi]_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"outerTenth", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 " the potential is diagonal in position, so its propagator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{"-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], " ", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 " is just a pointwise phase. Define a half-step of it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", 
    "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"Vfun", "[", 
       RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "\[Psi]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One requirement hides in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Vfun", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<x\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],
 ": the potential must accept the whole coordinate list at once. Any formula \
built from arithmetic and listable primitives (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"#", "^", "4"}], "/", "4"}], " ", "&"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Exp"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["Cos"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],
 ") qualifies automatically; a definition restricted to scalar arguments, \
such as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"v", "[", 
    RowBox[{"x_", "?", "NumericQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"x", "^", "4"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 ", does not, and needs a listable wrapper first."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's explain why the half-step. To approximate one step of the true \
dynamics, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], "+", 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],
 ", we use the Trotter-Suzuki formula: a family of operator-splitting methods \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"h", "B"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 " are each easy to compute but ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],
 " do not commute. Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 " are the kinetic and potential generators and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],
 ". The first-order member of the family of operator-splitting is the \
Lie-Trotter splitting, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "1"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "B"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ", with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],
 " per step and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],
 " over a fixed total time. The symmetric second-order member is the Strang \
splitting, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"h", "A"}], "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "/", "2"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 ", with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "3"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],
 " and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],
 ". More generally, higher-order Suzuki compositions give an order-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],
 " method with local error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 " and global error ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["O", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["h", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["p", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 ", the one lost power coming from the roughly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["h", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " steps needed to cover a fixed interval. We take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],
 ", the Strang splitting: with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["h", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", "\[HBar]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], "^"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "\[HBar]"}]], " ", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], " ", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", "\[HBar]"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],
 ", a half potential kick around a full kinetic drift, and it is exact \
whenever ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],
 ". One scope note: that second order belongs to the unitary substep by \
itself. The full conditional step will interleave the measurement update with \
this drift in one fixed order, and that outer splitting is first order in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"d", "t"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 "; the symmetric core is still worth having, since it is exact at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],
 " and costs only one extra pointwise phase."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"ift", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"\<p\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"dt", "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "mass", " ", "hbar"}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"ft", "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "dt_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", 
   "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "@*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"unitaryStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], " ", "@*", " ", 
    RowBox[{"potentialStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}]}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One full conditional step is now described as follows: draw an outcome, \
apply the Bayesian ",
 Cell[BoxData["measUpdate"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 ", then ",
 Cell[BoxData["evolveStep"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],
 ". Define the step:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", 
      " ", "xb_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"evolveStep", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"measUpdate", "[", 
      RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", " ", "xb"}], 
      "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:=",ExpressionUUID->"3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A whole experimental run is that step iterated ",
 Cell[BoxData["nt"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],
 " times from an initial state, with a fresh outcome drawn at each step. One \
runner does it: ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 " returns the sequence of conditional states and ",
 Cell[BoxData["Sow"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 "s each outcome as it goes. Define it:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "g_", ",", " ", "Vfun_", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]_", ",", " ", "dt_", ",", 
      " ", "nt_"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]0_", "]"}], " ", ":=", "\n", "   ", 
   RowBox[{"NestList", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"stepV", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "g", ",", " ", "Vfun", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt", ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sow", "@", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"drawSyntheticOutcome", "[", 
            RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]", ",", " ", "dt"}], "]"}], "[", 
           "#", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", 
     "\[Psi]0", ",", " ", "nt"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:=",ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Called inside ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reap"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["trajectory"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],
 " returns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"states", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "outcomes", "}"}]}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 ": the conditional states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 " and the stream of outcomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],
 ". Called bare, without ",
 Cell[BoxData["Reap"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 ", it returns only the states."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Those two outputs are the whole story; every other symbol from the glossary \
follows from the readings ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 " by simple steps. Rescale each reading by the known factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " to get the record increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], " ", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 ", and add these up for the running record ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 " if you ever need it. A running estimate over the stream of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 " recovers the mean position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],
 " (the filter of Part IV does this; in the simulation you can also read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],
 " straight off ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],
 ", which is how Part IV checks the estimate against the truth), and the mean \
then gives back the noise, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "=", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "-", "2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], " ", 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], " ", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],
 ". This just runs the generation backward: the simulation drew the noise and \
built the reading, and the chain from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 " undoes it, returning the exact noise from the true mean, or a leftover \
that is pure noise only when the model is right."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part III: The Free Particle: No Potential, Localizing and Heating\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's exercise the engine on the case we already understand analytically, \
the free particle, by passing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 " for the potential. The point is twofold: to see the generalized code \
reproduce the known free-particle physics, and to build the unconditional \
(master-equation) machinery we will reuse in the trap."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first known fact: under measurement a broad packet localizes to a \
steady conditional width ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],
 ". Set the free-particle stage first: a 256-point grid across a box of width \
50, unit measurement strength, a step of 0.005, and 600 of them."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
    RowBox[{"256", ",", " ", "50."}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]R", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"dt", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"nt", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell["\<\
Run one trajectory from a wide packet of width 2, with the noise seeded so \
the run repeats exactly:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"statesF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "11", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]R", ",", " ", "dt", ",", 
        " ", "nt"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "2."}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:=",ExpressionUUID->"5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],

Cell["\<\
Take the conditional width at each step, the square root of the position \
variance:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"widthsF", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"xVar", "[", 
       RowBox[{"gF", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     "statesF"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:=",ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the width and show it approaches the predicted steady value, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "/", "4", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"widthsF", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{".5", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nt", " ", "dt"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<conditional width\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<A broad packet localizes to the steady width (dashed)\>\""}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"Dashed", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
            "^", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"nt", " ", "dt"}], ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"hbar", "/", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"4", " ", "\[Lambda]R", " ", "mass"}], ")"}]}], ")"}], 
            "^", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:=",ExpressionUUID->"79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],

Cell[BoxData[
