Cell[TextData[{
 "Read the two curves by what an experiment could actually see. The solid \
curve is the two-point bet built from the noisy readings alone, so it is \
exactly what an observer holds: it starts at an even ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FractionBox["1", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],
 ", wanders, at first even leans toward the wrong lobe, then climbs to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 " as reading after reading accumulates and the state localizes to the left \
lobe. The dashed curve is a different kind of thing. It is the true fraction \
of the packet sitting in the left lobe, read straight off the grid state \
itself, and no experiment can see that state, so this curve is not \
observable: it is drawn only as the hidden truth to check the bet against. \
The two-point bet rides right on it, and the small gap between them is the \
price of treating each lobe as a single point, which for deciding ",
 StyleBox["which lobe", "TI"],
 " won costs almost nothing."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "That verdict was this run's; a different noise history would decide \
differently. The initial cat is symmetric, so nothing favors either lobe: the \
measurement forces a definite choice, but which lobe is set entirely by the \
noise. Overlay several independent seeded runs and watch their posteriors \
split, some pinning to ",
 Cell[BoxData["1"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],
 " (left), some to ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 " (right):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "k", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"LogisticSigmoid", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Accumulate", "[", 
         RowBox[{"logOdds", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
              RowBox[{"gC", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"0", " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "\[Lambda]C", ",", " ", 
               "dtC", ",", " ", "100"}], "]"}], "[", "\[Psi]Cat", "]"}], 
            "]"}], "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}],
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.1"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"0.5", ",", " ", "Gray"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<measurement step k\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\!\(\*SubscriptBox[\(P\), \(left\)]\)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Different runs, different verdicts\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:=",ExpressionUUID->"615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],

