Cell[TextData[{
 "Every grid value matches its predicted steady value to a fraction of a \
percent, the ratio column. The last row multiplies ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["x", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4156c81a-8a68-59d7-776d-e2442f1d2b3d"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalSigma]", 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e7ab4-00f8-e339-7ea6-73feb172ce03"],
 " and subtracts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["C", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b3ec616-de69-0141-3ac5-d853db1c53ab"],
 ": that combination equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c0d57bf-7ae8-3253-2433-4ef97e8280b9"],
 " only for a pure state, and the grid hits it. So the grid, which never \
assumed the state was Gaussian, produces exactly the pure squeezed Gaussian \
the algebra predicted, not just the right width."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0aaecb0d-dff0-cd78-3a55-e356d98a9442"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Reading the Position Out of the Noise", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"4fe4a286-576e-fd11-759b-3be06218c47b"],

Cell["\<\
The point of watching the particle is to know where it is. But the detector \
hands back something discouraging: a stream of position readings, each one \
almost pure noise. Can you recover the particle's mean position from that? \
You can, and the surprise is that you don't need the full wavefunction to do \
it, only five numbers, updated as each reading arrives. Those five numbers \
are themselves the conditional quantum state, its two means and three \
covariances; what you skip is the 256-amplitude grid, not the state. This \
five-number recipe is the quantum Kalman filter, the quantum form of the \
Kalman filter that turns a noisy signal into a running state estimate \
throughout engineering. It is what a trapped-nanoparticle or \
vibrating-membrane experiment does, inside a richer noise model: it never \
holds the full wavefunction, it watches the measured signal and runs this \
small calculation to know the mean position moment by moment.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"07179650-9fbb-2bc1-2d2c-081a1a4e792b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run one trajectory in the trap and keep every reading ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "_"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aecd320-e31f-2936-2a93-ca8d96aa781c"],
 " the detector produces:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"326b0854-5043-0b63-6268-a21e61f65649"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"recStates", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "recOuts", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "21", "]"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
        RowBox[{
        "gH", ",", " ", "Vharm", ",", " ", "\[Lambda]H", ",", " ", "dtH", ",",
          " ", "ntH"}], "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"gaussian", "[", 
        RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[CapitalSigma]xZP", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1d6edc53-4ce5-e0f2-4b15-d61d6491b2d8"],

Cell["\<\
Also keep the conditional mean the full grid computes, the reference the \
filter is checked against later:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"45f7e4e6-4e1c-a184-738c-fdc06baef3ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xGrid", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"xMean", "[", 
      RowBox[{"gH", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    "recStates"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[88]:=",ExpressionUUID->"70e98525-204e-6ba4-2096-1c8f51fb398e"],

Cell["\<\
Look at the readings on their own. Each scatters far wider than the \
conditional mean it carries, so the readings are mostly noise and the signal \
cannot be picked out by eye:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"704169dd-a4db-5005-207e-8086cd6e236f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"recOuts", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "tfH"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time t\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<reading\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<The readings: the conditional mean buried in noise\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[89]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7b2d1c14-5aff-cd5f-2ad2-965e5e8b97a5"],

