         Part[#, 2]]}& ), "CopiedValueFunction" -> ({
        (Identity[#]& )[
         Part[#, 1]], 
        (Identity[#]& )[
         Part[#, 2]]}& )}},
  PlotInteractivity:>True,
  PlotLabel->FormBox[
   "\"The price of inefficiency: the strength needed to beat the vacuum\"", 
    TraditionalForm],
  PlotRange->{{0., 0.999999981632653}, {0., 60.}},
  PlotRangeClipping->True,
  PlotRangePadding->{{
     Scaled[0.02], 
     Scaled[0.02]}, {0, 0}},
  Ticks->{Automatic, Automatic}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961740770052*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[102]=",ExpressionUUID->"fe539c8f-a53c-4b2e-93ce-b3a0e1b8a4ad"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now read the two numbers separately at the experiment's efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.34"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],
 " and the strength ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],
 " we ran. First the steady position variance in vacuum units, which now sits \
above one: at this efficiency the state is broader than the vacuum, not \
sharper."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"sqRatio", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}], " ", "\[Mu]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}]}], " ", "/.", " ", "harmNum"}], " ", 
  "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", "0.34"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[103]:=",ExpressionUUID->"12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],

Cell[BoxData["1.2894784443338756`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961740782975*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[103]=",ExpressionUUID->"8a583cc8-e788-48bb-8f33-344a96e9b6dd"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Then the threshold strength that would be needed to reach the vacuum at \
this efficiency, which lands far above the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"],
 " we actually ran."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"656925a1-dac3-d209-1316-bc0adf77a153"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"2", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
     RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", "\[Eta]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "^", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"3", "/", "2"}], ")"}]}]}]}], " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "->", " ", "0.34"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[104]:=",ExpressionUUID->"09e13884-5cc5-f650-3f9e-b1ee5571dcba"],

Cell[BoxData["8.195653482579244`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961740795864*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[104]=",ExpressionUUID->"c4a4be4b-92a7-4d1b-bc40-b01ffad460a2"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At that efficiency and that strength the conditional variance sits above \
the vacuum, and the threshold is far beyond our ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136212ad-a4c2-b9f3-4111-8bf6cd740bd9"],
 ": the same detector, made to watch harder, would push the state back under. \
That, not efficiency by itself, is what sets where an experiment lands, and \
the real figure carries thermal force noise and damping this model leaves out \
besides. What survives all of it is the shape of the answer: five numbers, \
driven by the record, running in the laboratory's real-time loop."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"67f6b273-a0bf-ee61-0d8d-343cd14bb54b"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Part V: Averaging Over Runs: A Trapped State That Never Settles\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"07a2a6c0-d7ac-3784-2d51-3fade25e9dee"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The conditional variance settled at its steady squeezed value. It is \
natural to expect the unconditional state, the average over the record, to \
settle too, perhaps into a thermal state. It does not, and seeing why is \
worth a moment. The trap conserves energy on its own, but the measurement \
backaction keeps injecting energy the closed trap has no way to remove. Watch \
this in the moments: the unconditional second moments close by themselves, \
and their energy has a constant source. Solve the unconditional moment \
equations in closed form and read the energy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d29df82-54ab-6c21-24d6-d6ec5d5e370b"],
 ":"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2673b224-f5d9-a24c-4e00-2b81fc6df096"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"XX", ",", " ", "SS", ",", " ", "PP"}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"usol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", 
    RowBox[{"DSolve", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"XX", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"SS", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"SS", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"PP", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", "m"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"m", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"XX", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"PP", "'"}], "[", "t", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "2"}], " ", "m", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"SS", "[", "t", "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
           RowBox[{"\[HBar]", "^", "2"}]}]}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"XX", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "xx0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SS", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"PP", "[", "0", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "pp0"}]}], "}"}], ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"XX", ",", " ", "SS", ",", " ", "PP"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "t"}],
      "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"energy", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PP", "[", "t", "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "m", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Omega]", "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"XX", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], " ", "/.", " ", "usol"}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[105]:=",ExpressionUUID->"27388ee6-22a7-f122-4ec7-27c05753c008"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  RowBox[{"pp0", "+", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], " ", "xx0", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]}], 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961741025941*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[107]=",ExpressionUUID->"7bced3ec-8c18-4da7-ae77-01e2c1a02fbe"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It is linear in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["t", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06a776cb-b9d0-3c58-2e5d-6f95386a86a2"],
 ", so its time derivative should be a constant, the steady heating rate:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7641b941-63e8-8619-1e7e-312b1582ed63"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"D", "[", 
   RowBox[{"energy", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[108]:=",ExpressionUUID->"42b8cf72-fa81-ffe6-7247-e73fff35c5cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FractionBox[
  RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}], 
  RowBox[{"2", " ", "m"}]]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961741030677*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[108]=",ExpressionUUID->"da3bb90d-f982-427c-92a1-2b1bb72b4cdf"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The energy is exactly linear in time, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], "0"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "473593be-64fb-e664-6eca-0af80c8fcd4e"],
 ", with no oscillatory part: the breathing of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79a8e286-b760-8808-2f57-fbe3c21adb52"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "766f3dde-6e6e-8ae3-1e14-b4980b18d8c9"],
 " against each other cancels in the sum, leaving only steady heating at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7acff19c-f8f8-c05b-2af4-e8d9f97292a1"],
 ". That rate is not the trap's. The dissipator feeds energy at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["[",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], 
      StyleBox["]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36bb0aa4-099e-3511-5e58-a30ea8289c7b"],
 ", and the double commutator is a pure number: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["p", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "/", "2", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "-", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fab4322-7f5b-c123-15a9-5a8c7aef9009"],
 ", since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "559c0528-76f1-864e-03a3-9d720285ec94"],
 " commutes with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c3b3e9a-7f95-6e09-75d8-b7c47a203553"],
 ". So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["E", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"], "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b834648-1855-f17e-29b1-581299e1c044"],
 " in any potential: position measurement is a constant-power heater whatever \
the landscape, and the trap merely makes the bookkeeping solvable in closed \
form. Equivalently, the mean occupation climbs linearly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[HBar]", "/", "2", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6aa15cf4-f328-f435-1a5f-55b186c2df1f"],
 ": the unconditional state is a mixed Gaussian whose energy and mean \
occupation grow without bound. With no damping and no detailed balance there \
is no thermodynamic temperature to assign, so it is thermal-like only in its \
Gaussian shape, not a thermal state. (The same closed solution with the trap \
switched off hands back the free particle of Part III:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1fa3178e-7287-38be-4550-8ee807338a84"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"XX", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"PP", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "/.", " ", "usol"}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[109]:=",ExpressionUUID->"33c53063-afff-c489-61fa-aa4cc98baed3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"xx0", "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["t", "2"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"3", " ", "pp0"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]}], ")"}]}], 
     RowBox[{"3", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}]]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"pp0", "+", 
    RowBox[{"t", " ", "\[Lambda]", " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[HBar]", "2"]}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961741440156*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[109]=",ExpressionUUID->"deede8f9-d93a-4993-92c8-8e919179cf71"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "with the initial second moments as the constants ",
 Cell[BoxData["xx0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20e38226-5aed-155d-5090-1b805e987fa7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["pp0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160727ef-d1b8-0069-3e3c-bec8e04d52b3"],
 ": the momentum law of Part III drops out below, and above it the position \
variance grows as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "261df1b1-b81e-57af-4e22-e8fb39ab3df5"],
 " at late times, the momentum random walk integrated twice.) Confirm it on \
the grid by propagating the master equation and reading the energy and the \
individual moments at a few times. First two observables on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00ba9d2f-c328-50fc-3059-1488f6dd22c6"],
 ", position-squared as a diagonal expectation and the energy:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"02964792-f196-8b6e-32ae-5edf8020d9b4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gHL", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"grid", "[", 
