Cell[TextData[{
 "The two curves part company exactly when probability reaches the top of the \
momentum ladder, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Rho]pTail"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6afe19ed-5a5e-331e-1a85-90b75fe89e64"],
 " from Part III says so. At the start almost nothing sits in the fastest \
tenth of the momenta, so the grid is still faithful:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"142f588d-e120-bc70-3dd5-51d690da075a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]pTail", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"First", "@", "\[Rho]long"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[123]:=",ExpressionUUID->"029948d8-232c-2201-32a7-618256d9716b"],

Cell[BoxData["1.405450190338988`*^-16"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9949617425374804`*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[123]=",ExpressionUUID->"e98c3b69-f0dd-497b-8289-7b0fd00c2f84"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
By the end enough has piled into that momentum tail for the grid to break \
down, exactly where the two curves parted:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"32f703b9-71e1-95eb-628c-9ae30795ff31"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"\[Rho]pTail", "[", 
  RowBox[{"gS", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Last", "@", "\[Rho]long"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[124]:=",ExpressionUUID->"0c860bbc-8d1f-f590-34bd-a2e624abdffa"],

Cell[BoxData["0.07243236114446928`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.994961742551631*^9},
 CellLabel->
  "Out[124]=",ExpressionUUID->"6541f5db-3804-4d84-9e45-5c32badcb988"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
From there on the small grid is lying about the continuum, the honest content \
of every cutoff warning above. The trap's ramp, plotted before this caveat, \
sits inside its safe window, so it carries no such lie.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"74b37722-3fdc-1a4f-1c41-6e8cba696895"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A genuine thermal ",
 StyleBox["steady", "TI"],
 " state needs a mechanical damping channel to balance that input, which is \
exactly why the optomechanics experiments cool with feedback rather than \
watch the bare measurement; adding that channel to the master equation is the \
natural next extension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"31781dc2-1028-33d4-6707-94aca1c2813e"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
